    <statement><p>Given that <m>P(91) = 43</m> and <m>P'(91) = 16</m>, approximate
<m>P(95)</m>.</p>
<p><m>P(95) \approx</m> <fillin characters="6" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>107</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><alert> Solution:</alert> 



Using the formula, <m>f(c + h) \approx f(c) + f'(c)\cdot h</m>, with 
the function <m>P</m>,
<me>P(95) = P(91 + 4) \approx P(91) + P'(91)\cdot (4)
  = 43 + 16 \cdot (4) = 107.</me>


</solution>
